" — and is needed for substitution","Composition expresses \"has-a\": an object holds helpers and delegates work to them","One main base plus mixins, not several equal bases; to reuse code, use a field"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Dog","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Animal","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":142.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":216.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"text":"is-a","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Car","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Engine","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":142.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":216.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":56.0,"text":"has-a","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"1 main base","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"+ mixins","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"otherwise — composition","size":10.5}]],"cues":[13.6,22.3]}]},{"title":"Technical limits","sub":"Layout and names","short":"Limits","main":"__x is mangled to _Class__x.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Memory layout","Name clashes","Name mangling"],"captions":["If two parents have different memory layouts (both with slots), a subclass can't be created","Identical attribute names in different parents lead to silent overwrites","Names with two leading underscores are mangled: __x in class A becomes _A__x and doesn't clash"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["class A: __slots__ = ('x',)","class B: __slots__ = ('y',)","class C(A, B): ...","# TypeError: multiple bases have","# instance lay-out conflict"],"hl":[2],"bad":[2,3,4],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"A: self.size","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"B: self.size","tone":"blue","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"w":110.0,"h":26.0,"text":"C — what size?","tone":"red","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":120.0,"y1":74.0,"x2":154.0,"y2":104.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":240.0,"y1":74.0,"x2":206.0,"y2":104.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["class A:","    def __init__(self):","        self.__x = 1","vars(A())   # {'_A__x': 1}"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}]],"cues":[13.5,21.8]}]},{"title":"Debugging a hierarchy","sub":"Printing the MRO","short":"Debugging","main":"Where a name is defined — the first class in the MRO with it in __dict__.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Print the order","inspect.getmro","Where defined"],"captions":["Print Cls.__mro__: you see who comes after whom","inspect.getmro(Cls) and help(Cls) show the same and list methods with their source","Where is a name defined? — the first class in the MRO with it in its own __dict__"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["print(Model.__mro__)","# (Model, LogMixin, Base, object)"],"hl":[0],"lang":"python","size":11.5,"lh":30.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["inspect.getmro(Model)","help(Model)"],"lang":"python","size":11.5,"lh":30.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["for cls in Model.__mro__:","    if 'save' in vars(cls):","        print(cls.__name__)","        break"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[10.7,23.4]}]},{"title":"ABC, Protocol, Generic","sub":"Same rules","short":"ABC and Protocol","main":"Look at the whole MRO.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Abstract","Protocols and Generic","Whole order"],"captions":["An abstract class is an ordinary part of the MRO, but its metaclass ABCMeta is inherited","Protocol and Generic also sit among a class's bases and enter the MRO","When reading a complex hierarchy, look at the whole order, not one definition line"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"ABC","tone":"yellow","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"ABCMeta","tone":"yellow","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":146.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":210.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"dash":"3 3","width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["class Repo(Generic[T], Storage):","    ...","Repo.__mro__","# Repo, Generic, Storage, ..."],"hl":[3],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m0","x":44.0,"y":70.0,"w":60.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Repo","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m1","x":112.0,"y":70.0,"w":60.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Generic","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m2","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":60.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Storage","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m3","x":248.0,"y":70.0,"w":60.0,"h":26.0,"text":"ABC","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m4","x":316.0,"y":70.0,"w":60.0,"h":26.0,"text":"object","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"text":"the whole order in view","size":10.0}]],"cues":[12.1,22.5]}]},{"title":"Common mistakes","sub":"What to avoid","short":"Mistakes","main":"Hard to answer? Simplify.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Call by name","Forgot kwargs","Too complex"],"captions":["Parent.method(self) in a diamond instead of super() — the common ancestor runs twice","A mixin without **kwargs in __init__ breaks the chain; a mixin with its own state becomes an ordinary parent","Can't say which method is called — the hierarchy is too complex: simplify or use composition"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["class B(A):","    def f(self):","        A.f(self)   # twice in a diamond"],"hl":[2],"bad":[2],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["class Mixin:","    def __init__(self, name):","        self.name = name   # no super()"],"bad":[1,2],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m0","x":50.0,"y":54.0,"w":84.0,"h":26.0,"text":"C1","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m1","x":150.0,"y":54.0,"w":84.0,"h":26.0,"text":"C2","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m2","x":250.0,"y":54.0,"w":84.0,"h":26.0,"text":"C3","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m3","x":50.0,"y":94.0,"w":84.0,"h":26.0,"text":"C4","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m4","x":150.0,"y":94.0,"w":84.0,"h":26.0,"text":"C5","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m5","x":250.0,"y":94.0,"w":84.0,"h":26.0,"text":"C6","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":132.0,"text":"what is called? unclear","tone":"red","size":10.5}]],"cues":[12.1,24.2]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"Class design","short":"Summary","main":"MRO, super, mixins and composition.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["MRO","super","Mixins","Caution"],"captions":["An attribute is found via the MRO: C3, each class once, children before parents, base order kept","super() is the next class in the MRO; methods cooperative, __init__ with **kwargs","Mixins go left; one main base","Prefer composition, keep hierarchies shallow, check complex cases by printing the MRO"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"A","x":180.0,"y":28.0,"w":54.0,"h":24.0,"text":"A","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"B","x":106.0,"y":78.